WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.910
Open-source contributors and grant-funded
developers need to show which team accepted their code.

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:15.094
Atesta gives project maintainers and grant programmes a
way to issue a credential for a specific GitHub contribution.

00:00:15.444 --> 00:00:22.769
This demo uses fictional people and an
organisation, but its public NEAR testnet token is real.

00:00:24.081 --> 00:00:28.726
The first check confirms the
public record matches its digest.

00:00:29.075 --> 00:00:35.690
The second reads the live NEAR
testnet contract. It holds the same digest.

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:45.938
The credential is active and non-transferable. The page names
the issuer and holder and links to the real mint transaction.

00:00:46.288 --> 00:00:51.492
NEAR anchors this record
publicly, so anyone can check it later.

00:00:52.795 --> 00:01:00.935
This can help open-source maintainers, grant reviewers and
developer portfolio builders check a specific endorsement.

00:01:01.285 --> 00:01:13.919
In real use, the authorised organisation makes the decision. This sample shows
how anyone can check the record. Try the live demo and inspect the repository.
